----- stdout -----
A declarative interface for every secret provider. https://monosecret.dev

Usage: monosecret [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init      Initialize a new monosecret.toml (optionally, from a provider)
  add       Add a secret declaration to monosecret.toml (0.18+)
  set       Set a secret value
  get       Get a secret value
  delete    Delete stored secret values from a provider (0.18+)
  run       Run a command with secrets injected
  manifest  Emit a secret-value-free manifest for SDK code generation
  export    Resolve secrets and print them for another tool to consume
  check     Check if all required secrets are in the provider, if not set them
  schema    Emit a JSON Schema for the manifest's typed shape
  config    Manage Monosecret configuration
  import    Import secrets from a provider to another provider
  cache     Manage cached provider values (0.17+)
  audit     Show the local audit log of secret access
  env       Load resolved secrets into a shell or CI environment
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -f, --file <FILE>      Path to monosecret.toml (default: auto-detect by walking up from current directory) [env: MONOSECRET_FILE=]
  -v, --verbose...       Increase diagnostic logging (`-v` for debug, `-vv` for trace). Can also use `RUST_LOG=debug` or `RUST_LOG=trace`
      --reason <REASON>  Reason for accessing secrets, recorded by providers that support audit logging (e.g. Proton Pass agent sessions). Takes precedence over the PROTON_PASS_AGENT_REASON environment variable [env: MONOSECRET_REASON=]
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

----- stderr -----
